Package: CBAMMR
Type: Package
Title: Comprehensive Bayesian and Advanced Meta-Analysis Methods in R
Version: 9.0.0
Date: 2025-11-05
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mahmood", "Developer", email = "mahmood726@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Claude", "AI", role = "ctb")
    )
Description: Integrated workflow package for meta-analysis building on established tools
    (metafor, meta, RoBMA). Provides three key contributions: (1) Workflow automation through
    cbamm_auto() function that standardizes analytical decisions by automatically detecting data
    types, calculating effect sizes via metafor::escalc(), selecting appropriate methods, and
    generating reproducible reports; (2) Clinical decision support tools including fragility
    indices, baseline-risk-specific NNT calculations, and decision curve analysis integration;
    (3) Transportability weighting using entropy balancing to adjust meta-analytic estimates
    for target populations. Includes effect size calculation (wrapping metafor, supporting 40+
    measures), heterogeneity assessment (Q, I², H², tau²), publication bias methods (Egger,
    Begg, trim-and-fill, PET-PEESE via existing packages), Bayesian approaches (via brms/RoBMA),
    and automated GRADE/PRISMA 2020 reporting. Ten example datasets demonstrate common meta-analysis
    scenarios. Aims to improve reproducibility through standardized workflows while maintaining
    transparency in methodological choices. Users seeking advanced customization should consider
    using metafor or meta packages directly.
